**What the null teaches.** Neither a trend meter nor a vol meter describes when wall-to-wall runs. More important, the in-sample ER-top group shows no continuation effect at all, and out-of-sample the effect is positive in every ER quintile. So the continuation is a property of the era, not of a detectable regime state, and ER cannot be used to anticipate when it switches. One side fact: about two thirds of reaccel entries already point with the prior 24h move, so the effect comes mostly from the minority of counter-direction entries failing.

