**The structural finding came from the post-hoc description.** In index points the Dukascopy US100 spread is an administered schedule, not a liquidity signal. It sat at a fixed 3.44 pt off-hours and 1.44 pt during US cash hours for 44 straight months, then stepped to a flat 1.15 pt at every hour from September 2025. The out-of-sample window straddled that step, which is why the profile correlation failed. In the latest regime, gold's fixed 0.16 USD spread is cheaper than US100 at every hour relative to the median 5-minute move, and a projected wall-to-wall cost is roughly 0.020 R for gold against 0.039 R for US100. Gold's own relative cost fell to a quarter of its 2022 level because a fixed nominal spread shrinks as price and volatility rise.

**Strongest counter-argument recorded.** All of this describes the Dukascopy feed, not the account's US100 pricing. The account's gold is a fixed 0.16 USD unlike Dukascopy, so its US100 may also be a different fixed value with no off-hours penalty. The comparison is unconfirmed until the one-time read-only MT5 probe records the account's US100 spread, logged as needs-data with high priority.

