| Recent 2024-26 | 0.83 | −0.018 (−0.13) | +0.018 (+0.23) |

**The structural fact that drives the result.** Gold's daily correlation with nominal yields was negative on 97 to 100 percent of days every year from 2014 through 2024. So "rate-driven period" cannot separate 2021-22, where the effect was zero, from 2024-25, where it peaked. The correlation then weakens toward zero in 2025 and 2026H1, exactly when the effect is strongest. The pre-written reading (ii) applies: the 2024-25 localization is not explained by gold reacting to rates at the daily scale, which also weakens the "rates drive gold drift" mechanism that cycle 13 already found only half-funded.

