**Results (pre-registered, out-of-sample 2021-26H1, day-clustered SE):**

| Statistic | 外 2021-26H1 | 在 2013-20 |
|---|---|---|
| Trades alive across the break | 811 of 7708 (10.5%) | 886 |
| Receipt coefficient b (remaining path on pop in R) | +0.76 (t 5.3) PASS | +0.84 (t 5.7) |
| Selection c (BUY-alive pop minus SELL-alive pop, halved) | −0.009R (t −0.65, MDE 0.029R) null | −0.022R (t −2.5) paying side |
| Net pop received per crossing trade | −0.003R (t −0.2) | −0.024R (t −2.7) |
| Share of window total R* | 1.6% | 18% |

Path-to-grid alignment was verified first at 100% (1592 of 1592 within 0.02 USD), so the bar-index time mapping holds intraday. The placebo window at 11:50 ET gave the same receipt coefficient, confirming the method.

**Conclusion.** The reopen pop is received mechanically by trades that cross the break, but only one in ten trades does, and the side-signed net is zero out of sample. The market-structure anomaly does not feed the strategy's R. In-sample it actually cost the book: SELL positions survived into days with large pops, paying about a fifth of the window's losses.

**Strongest counter-argument recorded.** The out-of-sample null has a detection limit of 0.029R, and the in-sample effect of −0.022R sits inside it. Single years 2021 and 2024 show the paying-side selection at t −3.5, while 2025 and 2026H1 flip positive. The data cannot distinguish "selection vanished" from "selection persists at in-sample size and is masked by two bull years."

