**What was tested**
Gold's own intraday autocorrelation structure, measured as Lo–MacKinlay variance ratios at 1h, 4h and 12h horizons on the existing M5 close cache, by year and by era. Secondary pre-registered cell: does the previous month's VR(48) condition the next month's mean wall-to-wall R*. Runtime 52 seconds, no scan, no MT5, no external calls.

**Results (both null)**

| Test | In-sample 2010-20 | Out-of-sample 2021-26H1 | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| Yearly VR(48) mean | 1.050 | 1.042 | diff −0.008, t −0.19, MDE 0.082 |
| Prev-month VR48 → next-month R*̄ (β per 1 sd) | −0.0065R, t −0.72 | −0.0016R, t −0.13, perm p 0.92 | null, MDE 0.018 / 0.025R |
| Positive control (inject +0.05R) | t +3.22 | t +2.95 | method detects |

**Structural knowledge gained**
- Gold M5 is close to a random walk at 1h to 12h in 2021-26 (all VR z below 1). The weak multi-hour positive autocorrelation sits in 2010-20 instead (VR144 1.100, z 3.7). So the "edge lives in the recent regime" story cannot be explained by unconditional intraday trendiness.
- The 5-minute lag-1 negative autocorrelation (ρ1 −0.019, t −6.2, significant every year 2014-20) disappeared after 2021. Descriptive, bid-only series, mechanism unidentified.
- Monthly VR48 has lag-1 autocorrelation of only +0.05, so intraday trendiness is not a persistent monthly state.
- Together with cycle 9, meters built from gold's own series statistics (daily ER, volatility, intraday VR) carry no information about wall-to-wall outcomes. The line is closed in the backlog.

**Strongest counter-argument recorded**
Unconditional VR does not test conditional momentum after a wall break. Local post-break autocorrelation could exist while being offset elsewhere, leaving VR near 1. The monthly VR proxy is also mostly estimation noise, so the conditioning null is attenuated by errors-in-variables. Revival condition is logged: conditional post-break autocorrelation positive out-of-sample at t ≥ 2.

