**Knowledge gained.** Gold carries a positive volatility risk premium of the same size as equities in-sample, present 16 of 17 years, but it shrank in the recent window and turned negative in 2026H1 when realized vol overshot implied. GVZ is an efficient forecast that fully subsumes trailing realized vol out-of-sample. The premium does not predict returns at a 21-day horizon, and the literature effect is absent in our US500 series too.

**Strongest counter-argument recorded.** The PASS is not a harvestable edge: we hold no options instrument or chain data, the premium is compensation for vol spikes, and one bad half-year erases roughly a year of premium. In variance units the recent window is zero.

**Post-hoc supplement** (c34b, labelled look-ahead): the wall-to-wall scan is nearly vol-neutral. Its exposure to realized-vol surprise explains at most 0.012R of the −0.058R unconditional expectation, so "breakouts pay the insurance premium" is not the mechanism.

